abel\nbranch 'ci/pit-from-pr-label' set up to track 'origin/ci/pit-from-pr-label'.\n","code":0},{"id":15,"traceSequence":17,"command":"gh \"pr\" \"list\" \"--state\" \"open\" \"--limit\" \"1\" \"--head\" \"ci/pit-from-pr-label\" \"--json\" \"number,url\"","status":"done","output":"[]\n","code":0},{"id":16,"traceSequence":18,"command":"gh \"pr\" \"create\" \"--title\" \"ci(pi-assistant): load a labelled PR's Pit to test it on a live thread\" \"--body\" \"Lets a Pit change be tried on a real pi-action thread before it's merged and released, as #397 needs.\\n\\n## How\\n\\nA new `Choose the Pit extension` step in `pi-assistant.yml` picks the `extensions` input:\\n\\n- If the thread is a pull request labelled **`pi:pit-from-pr`** whose head is in this repository, pi loads `github:cv/pit#<head sha>`. The SHA is resolved when the job starts, so the tools don't change under pi during the run, even if it pushes to the branch. A `::notice` in the job summary names the commit it loaded.\\n- Otherwise it loads `github:cv/pit#v0.37.0`, as before.\\n\\npi-action installs extensions without lifecycle scripts, the same way it installs a tag, so any commit works like a release.\\n\\n## Safety\\n\\n- Fork PRs never qualify (head repository check), and only people with triage access can add a label.\\n- Only OWNER/MEMBER can start a run, which hasn't changed.\\n- If the lookup fails, the step falls back to the release.\\n\\n## Trying #397 once this is merged\\n\\n1. Add `pi:pit-from-pr` to #397. Its thread already has several runs and is far past `minTokens`.\\n2. Comment `@pi` twice. After the first run answers, its `afterRun` collapses the older runs. The second run's first prompt should be much smaller, and `session.outline()` should show `elided` entries starting `[Pit: collapsed`.\\n3. Remove the label to go back to the release.\\n\\nThe workflow file is read from `main` for comment events, so this needs merging on its own, but #397 doesn't.\" \"--base\" \"main\" \"--head\" \"ci/pit-from-pr-label\"","status":"done","output":"https://github.com/cv/pit/pull/398\n","code":0}],"traces":[{"id":1,"sequence":1,"namespace":"shell","method":"exec","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":122}],"startedAt":1794909128704,"status":"succeeded","durationMs":77},{"id":2,"sequence":2,"namespace":"shell","method":"exec","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":145}],"startedAt":1794909128781,"status":"succeeded","durationMs":483},{"id":3,"sequence":3,"namespace":"__pit","method":"savedFunctionRun","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":24}],"startedAt":1794909129265,"status":"succeeded","function":{"invocationId":1,"name":"delivery.openPullRequest","scope":"project","depth":1},"durationMs":0},{"id":4,"sequence":4,"namespace":"shell","method":"execFile","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":3},{"type":"array","size":3},{"type":"object","size":1}],"startedAt":1794909129265,"status":"succeeded","function":{"invocationId":2,"parentInvocationId":1,"name":"git.revParse","scope":"global","depth":2},"durationMs":8},{"id":5,"sequence":5,"namespace":"shell","method":"execFile","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":3},{"type":"array","size":3},{"type":"object","size":1}],"startedAt":1794909129273,"status":"succeeded","function":{"invocationId":3,"parentInvocationId":1,"name":"git.switchBranch","scope":"global","depth":2},"durationMs":7},{"id":6,"sequence":6,"namespace":"__pit","method":"savedFunctionRun","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":15}],"startedAt":1794909129280,"status":"succeeded","function":{"invocationId":4,"parentInvocationId":1,"name":"delivery.commit","scope":"project","depth":2},"durationMs":0},{"id":7,"sequence":7,"namespace":"shell","method":"execFile","arguments":[{"type":"string","size":3},{"type":"array","size":4},{"type":"object","size":3}],"startedAt":1794909129281,"status":"succeeded","function":{"invocationId":4,"parentInvocationId":1,"name":"delivery.commit","scope":"project","depth":2},"durationMs":5},{"id":8,"sequence":8,"namespace":"shell","method":